# Cache manifest

What `cache/` holds and how to use it. The rules behind it are in
[../docs/discipline/results-cache.md](../docs/discipline/results-cache.md).

## Key

The key columns and the optional canonicalizer are set in `project.toml` under `[cache]`.
Record here, in words, what a key names and what makes two keys "the same object", so a
reader can check the canonicalizer does what it claims:

The owner or the first agent to cache a value fills this in and sets `[cache] key_columns` to
match.

- Key columns: _(fill in: e.g. "graph6")_
- Same object when: _(fill in: e.g. "the graphs are isomorphic")_
- Canonicalizer: _(fill in: the command, and what normal form it returns)_

## Tables

| Table | Quantities | Produced by | Cost per row | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| _(e.g. `results/chromatic.tsv`)_ | _(e.g. `chromatic_number`, `cost_seconds`)_ | _(script or experiment)_ | _(e.g. "~1 s at 30 vertices")_ | |

Every table is tab-separated with the header `<key columns> quantity value provenance date`.
{{#if modules.experiments}}
Experiments may keep their own table at `experiments/<slug>/results-catalog.tsv` in the same
format; `bin/cache lookup` reads those too, so they need no row here.
{{/if}}

## Commands

```
bin/cache lookup <key...> [--quantity Q]
bin/cache append cache/results/<table>.tsv <key...> <quantity> <value> <provenance> [--force]
bin/cache coverage
```
